    {
      "id": "navigation-distances",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Four distances",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": -280
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "Four distances",
        "body": "These are the steps a click moves through. Each is something you can see on screen, not a mode.\n\n- **Workspace.** Several graphs in view. Each is a mark, an icon or a card, with trunks between them.\n- **Graph.** One graph fills the view. Its ground, its nodes and its edges are what you see.\n- **Node.** One node has focus and is large enough to read.\n- **Inside.** You are working with what the node holds: scrolling its text, following its links.",
