    {
      "id": "navigation-click",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "What a click does",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "What a click does",
        "body": "For each kind of thing: what a click does at each of the three steps of rule 1, and what a drag does.\n\n## A graph’s tile\n\n- **Far or small:** The camera comes to it and frames it.\n- **In view:** You enter it. It becomes the graph you are in.\n- **Already has focus:** Nothing more.\n- **Drag:** By its title bar, moves the tile. By its body, pans.\n\n## A tile’s title bar\n\n- **Far or small:** Selects the graph without entering it, for closing, tidying or capturing.\n- **In view:** The same.\n- **Already has focus:** The same.\n- **Drag:** Moves the tile.\n\n## A node\n\n- **Far or small:** The camera comes to it.\n- **In view:** It takes focus and is brought to reading size.\n- **Already has focus:** You are inside it: its text scrolls, its links answer.\n- **Drag:** Moves it. If it is pinned, pans.\n\n## A Portal\n\n- **Far or small:** The camera comes to it.\n- **In view:** It takes focus, and shows the face of the graph it opens.\n- **Already has focus:** You go through. The graph opens beside this one and the camera travels to the other end of the connection: the Port the Portal opens onto, or the graph as a whole when it names none.\n- **Drag:** Moves it.\n\n## A link in text, or a Portal-style card\n\n- **A click:** you go through, as with a Portal. One click, because you are already inside the page.\n\n## The ground\n\n- **Far or small:** As a click on its graph’s tile.\n- **In view:** Focus returns to the graph as a whole. No node is selected.\n- **Already has focus:** The same.\n- **Drag:** Pans. By its title bar, moves it.\n\n## An edge inside a graph\n\n- **Far or small:** The camera frames both of its ends.\n- **In view:** It is selected, and its two ends are lit.\n- **Already has focus:** You travel to the end you are not at.\n\n## A port on a node\n\n- **Far or small:** As a click on its node.\n- **In view, or already in focus:** You follow its edge to the node at the other end.\n\n## A trunk between two graphs\n\n- **Far or small:** The camera frames both graphs.\n- **In view:** The stroke under the pointer is selected. Its wraps and ports are lit.\n- **Already has focus:** You travel to the graph you are not in.\n\n## An edge’s name\n\nAn edge shows its name when you are near it or have selected it. A click on the name goes through to the edge’s own graph: the graph that describes this relationship, or failing that the page of its class.\n\n## A handle on a tile’s border\n\n- **A click, at any distance:** you travel to the graph it faces.\n\n## A port on a tile’s border\n\n- **A click, at any distance:** you travel to the node that owns it, inside its graph.\n\n## Empty space\n\n- **Far or small:** Clears the selection.\n- **In view:** Steps out one level.\n- **Drag:** Pans.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "navigation-scheme"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any",
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any",
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "side": "top",
          "offset": 0.2,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
