    {
      "id": "navigation-back",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Going back, out, up and home",
      "position": {
        "x": 380,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "Going back, out, up and home",
        "body": "## Step out\n\nOne step further: out of a node to its graph, out of a graph to the workspace. Escape does the same. It is rule 2.\n\n## Back and Forward\n\nAlong the path you have travelled. Each stop is a graph, a node and a distance. Nothing opens or closes. A Portal is one end of a connection and the Port it opens onto is the other: going through puts you at the far end, and going back puts you at the end you left. This replaces a way-back Portal drawn into each graph.\n\n## The trail\n\nA line near the address bar that names the graphs you came through, oldest first. A click on a name travels there.\n\n## Up\n\nThere is no separate “up”. In the workspace you can see what this graph was opened from, by the trunk between them, and click it. So no graph has to declare a parent.\n\n## Home\n\nTravels to the root. Opens it if it is not open.\n\n## The address bar\n\nShows the address of the graph you are in. An address typed there opens beside what is already open, and the camera travels to it. The workspace is never replaced by accident.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "navigation-scheme"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any",
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any",
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "side": "top",
          "offset": 0.2,
          "position": {
