    {
      "id": "navigation-open",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Still to decide",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": 800
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "Still to decide",
        "body": "- **One click or two for a Portal.** This scheme takes two once it is in view: one to look at it, one to go through. A link in text takes one. If a Portal should also take one, it stops being a thing you can look at without leaving.\n- **How many graphs stay open.** If nothing closes by itself, a long walk leaves a long row of graphs. They could fade to marks with distance, or the oldest could close after some number.\n- **Whether editing really needs a different third step,** or whether a Portal should be gone through the same way in both modes.\n- **What the trail shows** when you have looped back to a graph you already visited.\n- **Whether walking belongs on the arrow keys.**",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "navigation-scheme"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
